# Contact form delivery (EmailJS). Copy to .env.local and fill in.
# These three values are PUBLIC identifiers by design; they are bundled into the site.
# Never put an SMTP password or EmailJS private key here.
#
# One-time setup in the EmailJS dashboard (https://dashboard.emailjs.com):
#   1. Email Services → add a service (e.g. Gmail) connected to axiomforge.dev.03@gmail.com.
#   2. Email Templates → create a template:
#        To Email:  axiomforge.dev.03@gmail.com      (type it literally; do NOT use a variable)
#        Reply To:  {{reply_to}}
#        Subject:   [AXIOMFORGE] {{subject}}
#        Content:   {{form_title}}
#                   Name: {{from_name}}
#                   Email: {{reply_to}}
#                   Subject: {{subject}}
#                   Message:
#                   {{message}}
#      Use double braces only ({{ }}), so visitor text is escaped, never rendered as HTML.
#   3. Account → Security: restrict to your site's domain(s) under "Allowed origins".
#   4. Copy the Service ID, Template ID and Public Key below, then rebuild.
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
